# Raw input: Ultra high resolution monochrome photograph capturing the Teton Range in Wyoming during golden hour, showcasing Ansel Adams' signature dramatic landscape style. Majestic snow-capped peaks pierce a soft gradient sky, with the iconic Grand Teton's sharp ridges rendered in crisp detail against the deep shadowed valley below. Sunlight dramatically illuminates the granite cliffs, revealing intricate textures of wind-sculpted rock, glacial striations, and snowfields with crystalline clarity. The Snake River Valley unfolds in velvety mid-tones, dotted with silhouetted evergreen forests and wildflower meadows. Impeccable contrast amplifies the scene's grandeur: pure white snow caps against velvety black mountain shadows, with every rock formation and tree branch defined by meticulous grain. Mood is serene yet awe-inspiring, evoking timeless wilderness. Shot on large format film with digital scanning, the image features 8K resolution, rich tonal range, and authentic Adams-style chiaroscuro. Artistic tags: high dynamic range, cinematic composition, naturalist photography, film grain texture, monochrome masterwork.
